# Testing

- Use Vitest for unit and integration tests and Playwright for browser behavior.
- Test observable contracts and behavior, not implementation details.
- For UI changes, verify mobile and desktop plus navigation, loading, errors, stale state, invalid input, accessibility basics, and reduced motion where relevant.
- Add a regression test for fixed bugs when practical.
- Mock all external traffic. CI must never call Platform stage or require real credentials.
- Independently inspect, run, and reproduce behavior; never trust an implementation report.
- Report Passed, Failed, Not tested, Risks, recommended fixes, commands, and evidence.
- Do not weaken assertions, skip tests, or change production behavior merely to make a test pass.
- Never mark behavior as passed unless it was directly verified.
